{#
	The placeholder reference, as markup, in one place (XIV-4, XIV-38).

	Two pages draw this list — the document templates page and the email templates
	one — and they draw it from the same `DocumentMarkers`, so drawing it from two
	copies of the same eight lines of Twig would have been the second thing to keep
	in step after the marker set itself.

	Only the *list* is shared. The prose around it is not, and deliberately so: one
	page is telling somebody what to type into Word and the other what to type into
	a textarea, and a sentence that covered both would be a sentence that helped
	neither.
#}
{% macro list(markers) %}
	<dl class="row small mb-0">
		{% for marker in markers %}
			<dt class="col-6 fw-normal">
				<code>{{ marker.token }}</code>
			</dt>
			<dd class="col-6 text-body-secondary">{{ marker.label }}</dd>
		{% endfor %}
	</dl>
{% endmacro %}
